 <section class="wrap transformation" aria-labelledby="transformation-title"><p class="eyebrow">Process design / Conceptual model</p><h2 id="transformation-title">From handoffs to a connected workflow.</h2><p>This comparison summarizes the regulatory notice experience before and after modernization. It is an illustration, not an exact system diagram.</p><div class="transform-columns"><div><h3>Before / fragmented</h3><ol class="process-path"><li>Reports</li><li>Spreadsheet</li><li>Manual review</li><li>Assignment</li><li>Notice preparation</li><li>Sending and filing</li></ol></div><div><h3>After / connected</h3><ol class="process-path connected"><li>Database rules</li><li>Qualification</li><li>Automated workflows and deadlines</li><li>Integrated review</li><li>Delivery and filing</li></ol></div></div><p class="process-note">The process handles approximately 12,000 notices annually. A core identification query was reduced from about 20 minutes to about 1 minute. Annual hours-saved estimates are deliberately excluded pending validation.</p></section>
